{"id": "clm:65add1f23b51b5c7b0098e1bb876d3558e04dd17bcb8a71c998ec7cba4c075cf", "type": "statement", "text": "In __background_compact_should_skip, a tracked file is skipped when its last attempt did not shrink the file OR its recorded bytes_rewritten is strictly less than conn->background_compact.bytes_rewritten_ema, after earlier eligibility and retry-bypass checks. Equality alone does not trigger the below-average skip. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://github.com/wiredtiger/wiredtiger/blob/develop/src/conn/conn_compact.c", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Background-Compaction Skip/EMA Heuristic"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c09b98f58907e3d2468080b27d3bebc9869e198919dcd3446a7589fc955b9d36", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:ce307c57fae8373a91cc8d97f9b98465dd144d2cc974bd93c33add375e7701c9", "ev:fbedaf7970155da0ff3b81873ba486357112db67bb2ebddfd7e03ddec9cceb0e"]}
{"id": "clm:2ddf35c1464988a7291cfc1950b82ffcb7b5593b157f44d5d4415f901b678001", "type": "statement", "text": "An attempt succeeds when start_size minus end_size is positive. Concurrent growth can make an attempt unsuccessful even when it rewrites bytes. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://github.com/wiredtiger/wiredtiger/blob/develop/src/conn/conn_compact.c", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Background-Compaction Skip/EMA Heuristic"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c09b98f58907e3d2468080b27d3bebc9869e198919dcd3446a7589fc955b9d36", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:fbedaf7970155da0ff3b81873ba486357112db67bb2ebddfd7e03ddec9cceb0e"]}
{"id": "clm:90c477d32b3be78b84f57ff0fc6c4ee97ffab88b9ad01cf710c50fcb1aae29bc", "type": "statement", "text": "The architecture guide describes background compaction as using accumulated success statistics to focus on promising tables. The inspected source additionally shows that even a previously successful file can be skipped when its bytes rewritten is below the connection EMA. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://source.wiredtiger.com/develop/arch-compact.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Background-Compaction Skip/EMA Heuristic"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/wiredtiger/wiredtiger/blob/develop/src/conn/conn_compact.c"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c09b98f58907e3d2468080b27d3bebc9869e198919dcd3446a7589fc955b9d36", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:b71c5eb38495694e1b5d03734ea921a6615235958e0a227222987f11b243e7ca", "ev:ce307c57fae8373a91cc8d97f9b98465dd144d2cc974bd93c33add375e7701c9"]}
{"id": "clm:b061e6e7b494deb6d3f86c2abc1f28b51bef6f8610826d85a888d8189acd5fa4", "type": "statement", "text": "The inspected implementation stores the EMA on the connection and the last bytes_rewritten and success outcome in each file’s tracking record; the comparison therefore uses a shared average across files rather than a separate EMA per file. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://github.com/wiredtiger/wiredtiger/blob/develop/src/conn/conn_compact.c", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Background-Compaction Skip/EMA Heuristic"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c09b98f58907e3d2468080b27d3bebc9869e198919dcd3446a7589fc955b9d36", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:ce307c57fae8373a91cc8d97f9b98465dd144d2cc974bd93c33add375e7701c9", "ev:fbedaf7970155da0ff3b81873ba486357112db67bb2ebddfd7e03ddec9cceb0e"]}
{"id": "clm:8deb36963eecfde4b862f932b99f3de7f7c5ed45d221ceecea22ce0502cba7f3", "type": "statement", "text": "The inspected cleanup removes tracking records when the service is disabled, on exit, or when their recorded attempt time exceeds max_file_idle_time. The tracking lookup also discards a URI record when its stored file id differs from the metadata id, preventing reuse of an old file’s history for a replacement with the same URI. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://github.com/wiredtiger/wiredtiger/blob/develop/src/conn/conn_compact.c", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Background-Compaction Skip/EMA Heuristic"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c09b98f58907e3d2468080b27d3bebc9869e198919dcd3446a7589fc955b9d36", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:29cdd57fb9fa0057107b5f78814ad6daaa9b9caa1be5d36f53973fb1635273c8", "ev:425e54c608220e28777567c9a75394918a3bf40bdbcd55c9a76dd7a12d3aa5ca", "ev:5a3dfce34d43bfc9383392af966544a2c5a82c9d1f24c8191d33f66e8990bdcc", "ev:adb368433fe68680fccf8a5e877ea82e82d243a203826f382004cee1d419103b", "ev:e3298f83bc8d303d3cc054466ec6ea972c1569d9d9032006cb76de3d5c633d39", "ev:ee6b38c89859eb0eeb2523db956e5776d82c9b24a4e13cc79e4e9ebe822fd00f"]}
{"id": "clm:793f427df027b9130136be8d982695f098b65bb443572f47b611c6f644bc33fe", "type": "statement", "text": "In __wt_background_compact_end, successful shrinkage updates bytes_rewritten_ema to (uint64_t)(0.1 * compact_bytes_rewritten + 0.9 * previous_ema). The quantity averaged is bytes rewritten, not bytes recovered, elapsed time, or a benefit-to-cost ratio. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://github.com/wiredtiger/wiredtiger/blob/develop/src/conn/conn_compact.c", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Background-Compaction Skip/EMA Heuristic"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/third_party/wiredtiger/dist/stat_data.py"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c09b98f58907e3d2468080b27d3bebc9869e198919dcd3446a7589fc955b9d36", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:fbedaf7970155da0ff3b81873ba486357112db67bb2ebddfd7e03ddec9cceb0e"]}
{"id": "clm:fc9bb7be086ccf671830a502f50a0bdf1b4ecd6c05206546b49bb8b7a4688ea8", "type": "statement", "text": "An otherwise eligible file without a tracking record is attempted. For a tracked file, run_once bypasses the previous-outcome/EMA skip, and elapsed time greater than or equal to max_file_skip_time also bypasses it. prev_compact_time is set at the start of an attempt, so this elapsed-time comparison is measured from that recorded start. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://github.com/wiredtiger/wiredtiger/blob/develop/src/conn/conn_compact.c", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Background-Compaction Skip/EMA Heuristic"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c09b98f58907e3d2468080b27d3bebc9869e198919dcd3446a7589fc955b9d36", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:425e54c608220e28777567c9a75394918a3bf40bdbcd55c9a76dd7a12d3aa5ca", "ev:ce307c57fae8373a91cc8d97f9b98465dd144d2cc974bd93c33add375e7701c9"]}
{"id": "clm:c65e4403e741cb1502eaec3ce6820eb5b36f1bba10ed623da1983018bb890af4", "type": "statement", "text": "The architecture guide says background compaction uses historical statistics to favor tables likely to reclaim space and avoid unnecessary attempts; it also skips the initial system-wide checkpoint described for ordinary compaction. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://source.wiredtiger.com/develop/arch-compact.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Background-Compaction Skip/EMA Heuristic"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c09b98f58907e3d2468080b27d3bebc9869e198919dcd3446a7589fc955b9d36", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:b71c5eb38495694e1b5d03734ea921a6615235958e0a227222987f11b243e7ca", "ev:e8ab9cbef1d0b7bbd423503215c1d5a1919c4ec93303be8e23473fb24a455fb5"]}
{"id": "clm:d7a1e8140c420b7a81003d5526776d5b915901be7c91231bf2d13a178f85eb45", "type": "statement", "text": "The architecture guide requires cache dirty content excluding updates to be below eviction_dirty_trigger and overall cache content below eviction_trigger before processing the next table. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://source.wiredtiger.com/develop/arch-compact.html", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Background-Compaction Skip/EMA Heuristic"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c09b98f58907e3d2468080b27d3bebc9869e198919dcd3446a7589fc955b9d36", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:b71c5eb38495694e1b5d03734ea921a6615235958e0a227222987f11b243e7ca"]}
{"id": "clm:0009fe35ff71a61861137e149b611937a9526a1af801b2c6030034c4ad70820e", "type": "statement", "text": "Statistics distinguish background_compact_ema, described as moving average of bytes rewritten, from background_compact_bytes_recovered. background_compact_skipped_unsuccessful counts skips following unsuccessful or below-average compaction. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/third_party/wiredtiger/dist/stat_data.py", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Background-Compaction Skip/EMA Heuristic"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c09b98f58907e3d2468080b27d3bebc9869e198919dcd3446a7589fc955b9d36", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4395be7785c4db6b45c51b9b575b5d244aaffdb74a0b22a0d535436add892ffc"]}
{"id": "clm:818d7b85dc499da54b5b28ceb429b296a0e1a49186a692bf6a95ec9486dee3a7", "type": "statement", "text": "The cached autoCompact manual describes continuous-mode failed collections as temporarily skipped and retried after approximately one hour. This operator-facing description does not specify the source-level EMA formula or guarantee an exact retry deadline. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/command/autoCompact.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Background-Compaction Skip/EMA Heuristic"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c09b98f58907e3d2468080b27d3bebc9869e198919dcd3446a7589fc955b9d36", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:f65608a35f4b8cea87289aa49663256f4625aebf577ab686c3aa62820884905a"]}
{"id": "clm:4e4069557c93c2605bfe2b4df3851b93945c646c70e5d2197e4e7a5f14372ea8", "type": "statement", "text": "The EMA update is inside the bytes_recovered > 0 branch. An attempt that leaves the file unchanged or larger sets prev_compact_success=false and does not update the EMA, even if it rewrote bytes. Concurrent operations can grow the file while compaction does work. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://github.com/wiredtiger/wiredtiger/blob/develop/src/conn/conn_compact.c", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Background-Compaction Skip/EMA Heuristic"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c09b98f58907e3d2468080b27d3bebc9869e198919dcd3446a7589fc955b9d36", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:fbedaf7970155da0ff3b81873ba486357112db67bb2ebddfd7e03ddec9cceb0e"]}
{"id": "clm:88489ce1668975d9d85582357e2d7bf4a6edd2a889b7526fcd646c9a071254d8", "type": "statement", "text": "run_once does not bypass every skip: the inspected function checks exclusions, missing files or permission errors, and file_size <= WT_MEGABYTE before the run_once history bypass. Passing this scheduler predicate also does not guarantee actual space reclamation. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://github.com/wiredtiger/wiredtiger/blob/develop/src/conn/conn_compact.c", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Background-Compaction Skip/EMA Heuristic"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://source.wiredtiger.com/develop/arch-compact.html"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c09b98f58907e3d2468080b27d3bebc9869e198919dcd3446a7589fc955b9d36", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4e3290e2b5be9c666866d4cf4d824fd5ba60d22c403333ab8cc63dc747f88b5e", "ev:ce307c57fae8373a91cc8d97f9b98465dd144d2cc974bd93c33add375e7701c9"]}
{"id": "clm:71768e67b3763f4584e212f7215ac483c2d7d23ac8111cb5a5176331c8a4302e", "type": "statement", "text": "The metadata candidate walk consults tracked statistics before opening a data handle to avoid unnecessary attempts. Its skip path increments background_compact_skipped; the previous-outcome/EMA predicate additionally increments background_compact_skipped_unsuccessful, while background_compact_ema exposes the moving average of bytes rewritten. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-30)", "source_url": "https://github.com/wiredtiger/wiredtiger/blob/develop/src/conn/conn_compact.c", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Background-Compaction Skip/EMA Heuristic"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/src/third_party/wiredtiger/dist/stat_data.py"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:c09b98f58907e3d2468080b27d3bebc9869e198919dcd3446a7589fc955b9d36", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:4395be7785c4db6b45c51b9b575b5d244aaffdb74a0b22a0d535436add892ffc", "ev:ce307c57fae8373a91cc8d97f9b98465dd144d2cc974bd93c33add375e7701c9", "ev:e3298f83bc8d303d3cc054466ec6ea972c1569d9d9032006cb76de3d5c633d39", "ev:fbedaf7970155da0ff3b81873ba486357112db67bb2ebddfd7e03ddec9cceb0e"]}
